        "text": "A rhomb of bare N-BK7 glass totally reflects the beam twice at 54.6°. Each total internal reflection shifts the phase of s against p by about 45°,\nso the two together act as a quarter-wave plate. The delay comes from the index alone, which changes little with wavelength.",
